IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), SCHEDULES III to IX. Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- Schedules I and II are repealed ("[Repealed, SOR/2002-245, s. 3]", "[Repealed, SOR/85-39, s. 4]") and have no
-- data. Each other Schedule is carried as DATA: one named record per paragraph with the Schedule's own words
-- (generated from the text file by a script that reads it, so no word is retyped), gathered into a LIST in the
-- Schedule's own order (the pattern of the phrasebook, entries 1.10 and 9.8). The paragraphs that are already
-- repealed inside a Schedule (Schedule IV items 5(c) and 7(a); Schedule VII items 2, 4, 7, 10 to 12, 14 to 19;
-- Schedule VIII items 2, 4, 7, 10 to 12, 14 to 19) have no record.
-- The rules after the data say what the Schedules decide: whether a province or an organization or a country is
-- named, and whether an employment is one a Schedule sets out. They are keyed by the heading text of the item
-- (for example "Province of Ontario"): a mistyped key finds nothing, which the tests check Schedule by Schedule.
--
-- The words of Schedules IV, VI and VIII describe kinds of employment in prose. The rules cannot read prose, so a
-- rule that asks "is the employment set out in Schedule IV?" takes the paragraph that the caller says describes
-- the employment and a BOOLEAN for whether the employment meets that paragraph's words (an input, not a guess).

§ `Regulations, Schedules III to IX`

§§ `The record that carries a Schedule paragraph`

DECLARE `cr1 Schedule paragraph` HAS
    `the schedule` IS A STRING
    `the item heading` IS A STRING
    `the paragraph` IS A STRING
    `the words of the paragraph` IS A STRING

§§ `Schedule III (section 24): provinces whose employment is included`

-- src:900 | 1 Province of Ontario.
@ref Reg Schedule III, item 1 (src:900)
GIVETH A `cr1 Schedule paragraph`
`Schedule III, item 1` MEANS `cr1 Schedule paragraph` WITH
    `the schedule` IS "III"
    `the item heading` IS "Province of Ontario"
    `the paragraph` IS ""
    `the words of the paragraph` IS "1 Province of Ontario."

