§§ `What the Schedules decide`

-- Does a list of Schedule paragraphs name an item with this heading?
GIVEN schedule IS A LIST OF `cr1 Schedule paragraph`
      heading IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`cr1 helper: a Schedule names an item` schedule heading MEANS
    any (GIVEN item YIELD (item's `the item heading`) EQUALS heading) schedule

-- Schedule III (section 24) names nine provinces. Regulation 24(1) includes the employment of those provinces.
@ref Reg Schedule III (src:900-908)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule III — the province is named` heading MEANS
    `cr1 helper: a Schedule names an item` `Schedule III` heading

-- Schedule IV (section 24): the employment of a province set out in the Schedule is excepted from the inclusion
-- of regulation 24(1). The paragraph is the one the caller says describes the employment ("" for the one
-- unlettered paragraph of an item); the employment must meet that paragraph's words. In item 9 (New Brunswick)
-- the unlettered opening words introduce the lettered paragraphs, which list boards, "except the employment ...
-- whose duties require his full time attention and who receives for performing such duties a regular salary":
-- so only a lettered paragraph can set an employment out there, and not for a full-time salaried one.
@ref Reg Schedule IV (src:912-1000)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
      paragraph IS A STRING
      `the employment meets the words of that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duties require the person's full time attention and the person receives a regular salary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule IV — the employment is set out` heading paragraph `the employment meets the words of that paragraph` `the duties require the person's full time attention and the person receives a regular salary` MEANS
        `the employment meets the words of that paragraph`
    AND (any (GIVEN item YIELD ((item's `the item heading`) EQUALS heading) AND ((item's `the paragraph`) EQUALS paragraph)) `Schedule IV`)
    AND (    (heading EQUALS "Province of New Brunswick")
         IMPLIES (    (NOT (paragraph EQUALS ""))
                  AND (NOT `the duties require the person's full time attention and the person receives a regular salary`)))

-- Schedule V (section 25) names six international organizations.
@ref Reg Schedule V (src:1003-1008)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule V — the organization is named` heading MEANS
    `cr1 helper: a Schedule names an item` `Schedule V` heading

-- The facts about a person that Schedule VI turns on.
@ref Reg Schedule VI (src:1012-1040)
DECLARE `cr1 Person employed by an international organization` HAS
    `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of a Tax Convention to which Canada is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of an order of the Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen within the meaning of section 3 of the Citizenship Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an official of the Commonwealth of Learning` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Schedule VI (section 25): employment by the organization, set out for that organization, that is excepted
-- from regulation 25's inclusion. Items 1, 5 and 6 list four kinds of person, (a) to (d); items 2 and 3 list two,
-- (a) and (b); item 4 lists two, (a) and (b). Paragraph (d) of items 1, 5 and 6 reaches a person who is neither
-- a citizen nor a permanent resident. An organization not named in Schedule VI has no entry: NOTHING.
@ref Reg Schedule VI (src:1012-1040)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
      person IS A `cr1 Person employed by an international organization`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule VI — the employment is set out` heading person MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (    heading EQUALS "Northwest Atlantic Fisheries Organization"
             OR heading EQUALS "North Pacific Marine Science Organization"
             OR heading EQUALS "North Pacific Anadromous Fish Commission")
        THEN JUST (    (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of a Tax Convention to which Canada is a party`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of an order of the Governor in Council`)
                    OR (    (NOT (person's `a citizen within the meaning of section 3 of the Citizenship Act`))
                        AND (NOT (person's `a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration Act`))))
        IF (heading EQUALS "International Pacific Salmon Fisheries Commission" OR heading EQUALS "International North Pacific Fisheries Commission")
        THEN JUST (    (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of a Tax Convention to which Canada is a party`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`))
        IF heading EQUALS "Commonwealth of Learning"
        THEN JUST (    (person's `an official of the Commonwealth of Learning`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Schedule VII (section 26) names the governments whose employment in Canada regulation 26 includes.
@ref Reg Schedule VII (src:1043-1058)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule VII — the government is named` heading MEANS
    `cr1 helper: a Schedule names an item` `Schedule VII` heading

-- The facts about a person that Schedule VIII turns on.
@ref Reg Schedule VIII (src:1062-1100)
DECLARE `cr1 Person employed by a foreign government` HAS
    `a subject or citizen of New Zealand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the New Zealand-Canada Tax Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permanently resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributes to a pension plan of the French Republic, or has contributions made on their behalf to such a plan by the French Republic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from Canadian income tax` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `participates in the Civil Service Retirement System of the United States or another pension plan financed by the Government of the United States, has done so continuously since before October 1, 1983 and has elected not to participate in the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a locally engaged employee of the Government of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a national of Japan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a national of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the Canada-Japan Income Tax Convention Act, 1965` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `participates in the Government of Malaysia's non-contributory gratuity scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen of Senegal` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Schedule VIII (section 26): employment in Canada by the government, of a person who meets one of the listed
-- descriptions, is excepted from regulation 26's inclusion. A government not named in Schedule VIII has no entry:
-- NOTHING. Note Australia: "(a) is not a citizen of Canada; or (b) is not permanently resident in Canada" is
-- met by anyone who lacks either status, so only a person who is both is left included (finding in NOTES.md).
@ref Reg Schedule VIII (src:1062-1100)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
      person IS A `cr1 Person employed by a foreign government`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule VIII — the employment is set out` heading person MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF heading EQUALS "New Zealand"
        THEN JUST (    (person's `a subject or citizen of New Zealand`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the New Zealand-Canada Tax Convention`))
        IF heading EQUALS "Australia"
        THEN JUST (    (NOT (person's `a citizen of Canada`))
                    OR (NOT (person's `permanently resident in Canada`)))
        IF heading EQUALS "France"
        THEN JUST (    (person's `contributes to a pension plan of the French Republic, or has contributions made on their behalf to such a plan by the French Republic`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax`))
        IF heading EQUALS "United States"
        THEN JUST (    (person's `a citizen of the United States`)
                    OR (person's `participates in the Civil Service Retirement System of the United States or another pension plan financed by the Government of the United States, has done so continuously since before October 1, 1983 and has elected not to participate in the Canada Pension Plan`)
                    OR (NOT (person's `a locally engaged employee of the Government of the United States`)))
        IF heading EQUALS "Japan"
        THEN JUST (    (    (person's `a national of Japan`)
                        AND (NOT (person's `a national of Canada`))
                        AND (NOT (person's `permanently resident in Canada`)))
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of the Canada-Japan Income Tax Convention Act, 1965`))
        IF (heading EQUALS "India" OR heading EQUALS "South Africa")
        THEN JUST (    (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act`))
        IF heading EQUALS "Malaysia"
        THEN JUST (    (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`)
                    OR (person's `participates in the Government of Malaysia's non-contributory gratuity scheme`))
        IF heading EQUALS "Senegal"
        THEN JUST (    (    (person's `a citizen of Senegal`)
                        AND (NOT (person's `permanently resident in Canada`)))
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act`)
                    OR (person's `exempt from Canadian income tax by virtue of paragraph 149(1)(b) of the Income Tax Act`))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Schedule IX (section 86) lists, country by country, the agreements that regulation 86 applies. A country is
-- referred to when some row carries its heading.
@ref Reg Schedule IX (src:1104-1154)
GIVEN country IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule IX — the country has an agreement referred to` country MEANS
    `cr1 helper: a Schedule names an item` `Schedule IX` country
